-#     - To keep the swap visually obvious, each mapping pair is generated with
-#       fill_color != border_color. Otherwise the variant could collapse back to a
-#       plain fill and become indistinguishable from the source task.
-#     - Filled sprites still use unique border-key colors, so each hole has a clear
-#       palette lookup and does not need color-id ordering or hidden tie-breaks.
-#   implicit_assumption_review:
-#     - Old `_fill_enclosed_bg_regions` was safe to mutate `out` in place because
-#       only bg holes changed.
-#     - That assumption breaks here: recoloring the border of one hole before
-#       analyzing another hole from the same sprite would corrupt adjacency counts.
-#     - Therefore the solver now reads adjacency and border-connected pixels from
-#       the original input grid `g`, while writing results into a separate `out`.
-#     - Recoloring cannot blindly replace every occurrence of a border color in the
-#       grid, because palette cells reuse the same colors. The solver restricts the
-#       recolor flood to same-color pixels reachable from the specific hole's
